notes.body:
@LarsVoelker The UX is much better with this changes.

Some comments:
* The new icon is very similar to the auto-scroll icon, and it's hard to distinguish. Maybe something inspired by this?
> ![x-aggregation-view_2x](/uploads/2698f05091b98e4e27867b498ad9ad40/x-aggregation-view_2x.png){width=24 height=24}
* The new icon is still blurry (high resolution display) and it's bigger than the auto-scroll and color-packets. They must have the same size.
> ![Screenshot_2026-03-30_at_11.06.24](/uploads/07cee60374ed720a21acd2a43a92e85a/Screenshot_2026-03-30_at_11.06.24.png){width=128 height=34}
* Configuration does not belong in Capture because it's also used when loading files. Maybe create it's own page, like "Expert" and "Filter buttons".
* "displays frames grouped by" is more "display latest packet matching"?
* When testing I was interested to know how many packet matched one entry. Is this available somewhere?
* The number of displayed packets should be shown in the status bar, like when having a display filter.

The previous code assigned `recent.aggregation_view` twice, the first assignment was never used. It looks like this is fixed now.
```
    recent.aggregation_view = enable;
    recent.aggregation_view = register_tap_listener_aggregation();
```

